				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1580,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Gate asset deployment strategy behind $TierSchemeAssets env var\n\nIntroduce a build-time gating mechanism that selects between two asset deployment modes: Embedded (default, assets Brotli-compressed into the binary) and FileSystem (full disk layout in Contents/Resources/ served via the localhost plugin static_root fallback).\n\nIn build.rs, read $TierSchemeAssets (defaults to \"Embedded\") and mutate tauri.conf.json at build time:\n- Embedded: frontendDist=\"../Sky/Target\", bundle.resources holds only Cocoon-needed files (bootstrap, extensions, nls, node_modules, product.json).\n- FileSystem: frontendDist=null, bundle.resources maps the full Sky/Target/ tree (Browser, BrowserProxy, Bundled, vs/, _astro/, index.html, etc.).\n\nIn LocalhostPlugin.rs, wrap the static_root resolution and Builder.static_root() call in #[cfg(feature = \"TierSchemeAssetsFileSystem\")] so the disk-fallback code is compiled only when FileSystem mode is active. Add \"TierSchemeAssetsFileSystem\" to IsDeclaredTierFeature and remove \"FileSystem\" from IsDefaultTierValue so it now emits a cfg feature rather than being a silent default.\n\nThis completes the foundation laid by the Static/Application/ prefix refactoring, making the deployment mode selectable at build time via a single environment variable rather than manual tauri.conf.json editing.",
			"SHA": "a9e4b2d9bf9e3ed04251361f03325445f343e208"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T08:21:51Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1580,
				4
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Consolidate bundle resources under Static/Application prefix\n\nTransition the Tauri bundle layout from flat resource paths to a structured \"Static/Application/\" prefix, unifying the bundle and development directory trees under a single source of truth. This eliminates the mismatch between the flat bundle layout (Contents/Resources/extensions) and the monorepo layout (Sky/Target/Static/Application/extensions).\n\nIn tauri.conf.json, remap all resource entries to target \"Static/Application/...\" and set frontendDist to null so the dev server delegates to the localhost plugin's static_root disk fallback. Add static_root resolution in LocalhostPlugin.rs that probes both the production bundle path (../Resources/) and the monorepo dev path (../../../Sky/Target/).\n\nIn ScanPathConfigure.rs, register the new canonical extensions path (Resources/Static/Application/extensions) before the legacy flat paths, which are retained as fallbacks for existing development environments.\n\nLegacy flat paths remain functional during the transition, so existing dev runs and CI pipelines continue to work until all resource mapping is migrated.",
			"SHA": "58b34f8a23c47aec5c01e92c493060403c7159b4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T06:37:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1576,
				4
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Strip verbose build identifiers, restore compact names\n\nRevert the DevelopmentNodeEnvironment_MicrosoftVSCodeDependency verbose naming scheme introduced in the previous commit for Cargo.toml bin/lib/package names and tauri.conf.json identifier/productName. Replace identifier with the stable \"fiddee.editor.binary\" key and set productName to \"Mountain\".\n\nAlso collapse externalBin and targets arrays back to single-line format (reverting the formatting change from the previous commit) and delete the .Backup files that were created alongside the verbose identifiers.\n\nThe verbose identifiers were only needed during a transitional Electron-profile debugging phase and are no longer required for the production Rust/Tauri pipeline.",
			"SHA": "f3219cd8532d03baa1cef3f2a23e51c026653c44"
		}
	],
